NAME: Late EOD check
OWNER: Sales Manager
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every day at 3:03 PM and 8:03 PM
MILESTONE: 2
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/spike-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Late EOD check" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "Late EOD check: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/spike-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/spike-team/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.
Run record: end every run with one line in this month's file in /workspace/spike-team/log/: the time, "Late EOD check", and done, no change, not switched on, blocked (why) or failed (why), with counts. If you stopped at the switch check or the isolation guard, the line you wrote there is this run's record; don't add a second.

Use the eod-parsing skill. Re-read yesterday's EOD window including edits and thread replies, and compare it with /workspace/spike-team/data/eod/<yesterday>.json. If you can't read the channels, change nothing, post nothing and record the run as blocked. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop. If a late or edited EOD changed the totals: update the json, rebuild the summary, and in live mode post the corrected summary as a thread reply under the original (standing approval 5, timestamp in <yesterday>.posted); in preview send it to Dan. Then send Dan one line: "Updated: <rep> posted late, cash +$X." Also check today's window and record early posts so the morning run is faster.
Before each team post, run the slack-api skill's sent check, so nothing is posted twice.
